BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Siltwatch) Tj T* () Tj T* (Siltwatch: Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Street flooding in small towns is usually caused by something mundane: a catch basin packed) Tj T* (with sediment, leaves, and trash that can no longer take in water. Towns with fewer than 25,000) Tj T* (residents typically have between 300 and 1,500 catch basins and one or two public works) Tj T* (employees available to maintain them. Because nobody can see inside a basin without lifting the) Tj T* (grate, crews work from a fixed calendar, usually one pass per year, or respond after a resident) Tj T* (calls to report standing water. Both approaches fail in predictable ways. Calendar cleaning) Tj T* (spends labor on basins that are mostly clear, while the few that fill quickly, often those) Tj T* (downhill from construction or unpaved roads, clog between visits. Reactive cleaning means the) Tj T* (flood has already happened, along with the property damage, the emergency overtime, and the) Tj T* (complaints to the town council.) Tj T* () Tj T* (In interviews with 14 stormwater and public works managers in three states, 12 told us that an) Tj T* (inability to know which drains need attention is their primary maintenance problem. Eleven said) Tj T* (they had no budget for a full asset-management system, but all 14 said a low-cost tool that) Tj T* (pointed crews to the right drains would change how they schedule work.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Siltwatch is a solar-powered sensor and phone app. The sensor mounts under the grate inside a) Tj T* (catch basin. An ultrasonic ranging module measures the distance to the sediment surface and to) Tj T* (the water surface every 15 minutes. A small solar panel on the grate frame charges a battery) Tj T* (sized to run through two weeks of overcast weather, and the unit reports over a low-power) Tj T* (cellular connection that we manage, so towns do not need their own network or IT staff.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The app turns raw readings into a ranked list. Each instrumented basin receives a clog-risk) Tj T* (score based on sediment depth, the rate at which sediment is accumulating, and how slowly water) Tj T* (drains after rain. Crews open the app each morning and see the ten basins most in need of) Tj T* (cleaning. The app sends an alert when a basin crosses a threshold or when heavy rain is) Tj T* (forecast and a high-risk basin is still uncleaned. Each cleaning is logged with a timestamp and) Tj T* (a photo, which produces the maintenance records that towns must keep under their stormwater) Tj T* (permits.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our design priorities are low cost, no installation tools beyond a wrench, and a crew member) Tj T* (learning the app in under ten minutes. Our current prototype unit costs $62 to build in batches) Tj T* (of 100, and we project $41 at a volume of 1,000.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are roughly 19,000 incorporated places in the United States with populations under) Tj T* (25,000, and most are responsible for their own stormwater systems under federal permit) Tj T* (requirements. We estimate an average of 600 basins per town. Instrumenting even the highest-) Tj T* (risk 15 percent, about 90 basins per town, represents a serviceable market of roughly 1.7) Tj T* (million sensors. At our planned pricing, that is a long-term opportunity of about $400 million) Tj T* (in annual software revenue. Our initial focus is narrower: towns in the Midwest and Northeast) Tj T* (with populations between 3,000 and 20,000, a group of approximately 4,200 places where flooding) Tj T* (from clogged drains is a recurring council issue.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We sell each sensor for $149 and charge a software subscription of $60 per sensor per year,) Tj T* (which covers cellular data, cloud hosting, alerts, and compliance reports. A typical first) Tj T* (purchase is 40 sensors, or $5,960 in hardware plus $2,400 annually. Many towns can fund this) Tj T* (from a discretionary maintenance line without a bid process, which shortens the sales cycle. At) Tj T* (that pricing, hardware gross margin is 58 percent at current build cost and rises to about 72) Tj ET
