BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (percent at volume, while software margin is above 80 percent. We expect towns to expand) Tj T* (coverage after the first season, so subscription revenue per customer should grow without) Tj T* (additional selling cost.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (Large water-technology vendors sell level sensors and monitoring platforms aimed at city) Tj T* (utilities, at prices from $800 to $2,000 per node plus integration fees, which puts them out of) Tj T* (reach for our target towns. Some cities rely on smart-lid or camera-inspection services, which) Tj T* (are priced per visit and do not give continuous readings. Our real competitor is the status) Tj T* (quo: the annual calendar and the resident phone call. Our advantage is price, simplicity, and) Tj T* (focus on one decision, which basin to clean next. Our weakness is that we are new, our sensor) Tj T* (has been tested for months rather than years, and an established vendor could lower prices if) Tj T* (we prove the market. We believe our small-town focus and low support burden are hard for large) Tj T* (vendors to match.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Maya Okonkwo-Reyes, CEO, is a senior in civil and environmental engineering. She spent a summer) Tj T* (interning with a county stormwater division and conducted most of our customer interviews.) Tj T* (Daniel Trujillo, CTO, is a senior in electrical engineering who designed the sensor board and) Tj T* (power system. Priya Venkataraghavan, head of software, is a junior in computer science who) Tj T* (built the app and the risk-scoring model. All three work on Siltwatch part time alongside) Tj T* (coursework. We lack a founder with municipal sales experience, and recruiting an advisor with) Tj T* (that background is our top priority.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (Siltwatch LLC was formed this year. Our core concept was defined after the interview phase, and) Tj T* (we have since built three hardware revisions. We completed a pilot in two municipalities with) Tj T* (38 sensors installed for a full storm season. The sensors flagged 9 basins for early cleaning) Tj T* (before the heaviest rainfall; crews cleaned them, and neither town reported street flooding at) Tj T* (those sites. Sediment readings matched manual measurements within 1.5 centimeters in 31 spot) Tj T* (checks. One sensor failed due to a loose connector, which we fixed in the next revision. Both) Tj T* (pilot towns have told us they intend to buy, though neither has signed a purchase order, and) Tj T* (this is our largest gap.) Tj T* () Tj T* (To date we have spent $11,400, funded by $6,000 in founder contributions and a $5,400) Tj T* (university innovation grant. Over the next 12 months we project 6 paying towns and 240 sensors,) Tj T* (generating about $50,000 in revenue against $118,000 in costs, with break-even expected in the) Tj T* (third year as customers expand coverage.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are seeking $40,000 in prize funding. About $22,000 would pay for a first production run of) Tj T* (200 sensors and enclosure tooling, $10,000 for field certification and outdoor durability) Tj T* (testing through a full winter, and $8,000 for sales travel and conference attendance to reach) Tj T* (municipal buyers. Beyond funding, we are asking for introductions to experienced municipal) Tj T* (technology advisors and mentors who can help us convert our two pilot towns into signed) Tj T* (contracts and design a repeatable sales process.) Tj ET
